{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789936640,"nonce":"K4bzHZAzAGxAmOQGq7El7ON4/mg=","title":"cfg_simplify caps its work per call, forcing extra optimizer rounds","message":"`cfg_simplify::run` merges at most 32 block pairs and threads at most\n64 empty blocks per call. A function with more mergeable blocks than\nthat reports progress every round without finishing, and the optimizer\ndriver, which repeats its whole round while any pass reports progress,\nruns two or three rounds more than the function needs: each 10 ms on a\n1000-block body.\n\nFix: each merge and each threading removes a block, so the pass runs\nuntil nothing qualifies, bounded by the block count.","files":null}]}